{"file":{"content":"\\centering\n\\scriptsize\n\\caption{Contribution attribution (Part 2 of 40).}\n\\label{tab:contributions-2}\n\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.0}\n\\begin{tabular}{@{}clp{8.8cm}p{4.0cm}@{}}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{\\#} & \\textbf{Level} & \\textbf{Contribution} & \\textbf{Primary source} \\\\\n\\midrule\n25 & \\colorbox{red!25}{Critical}\n  & Almost-all crossing theorem: non-crosser density\n    $\\le e^{-0.1465\\,k}$; ensemble side fully closed;\n    architectural diagnosis (deterministic realization barrier)\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n26 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Exact cycle log correction $C(n) = O(1/n)$;\n    sufficient crossing criterion (succeeds for all\n    $n_0 \\le 5\\times 10^6$ except $\\{27,31,63\\}$)\n  & GPT (theorem) + Claude (verification + integration) \\\\[3pt]\n27 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Multi-cycle threshold analysis: $n^*/M$ decay,\n    $2^k{-}1$ hardest-start family, analytic obstruction\n    diagnosis for $n^* < M$ proof\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n28 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Universal one-cycle crossing: $n^*<1$ iff $r \\ge r_{\\mathrm{all}}(L)$;\n    $P_{\\mathrm{all},1\\mathrm{cyc}} = 0.4194$; $41.9\\%$ of odd starts\n    in classwise deterministic crossing blocks\n  & GPT (theorem) + Claude (verification + integration) \\\\[3pt]\n29 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Multi-cycle universal crossing: $R_k \\to 0$\n    exponentially by Kesten theory ($\\rho \\approx 0.84$);\n    classwise universal descent for a.e.\\ odd start\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n30 & \\colorbox{yellow!50}{Med}\n  & Route~A closure: adversarial $n^*$ grows $\\sim e^{0.023k}$,\n    proving all-blocks-universal approach impossible\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n31 & \\colorbox{yellow!50}{Med}\n  & Route~B obstruction: cycle-type autocorrelation\n    $\\rho(1) \\approx 0.20$, $\\rho(\\ell \\ge 2) \\approx 0$;\n    bit-generation blocks exhaustion argument;\n    $2^k{-}1$ termination theorem\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n32 & \\colorbox{yellow!50}{Med}\n  & Route~C obstruction: crossing-time ratio\n    $\\tau(n)/\\log_2 n \\le 7.8$ empirically;\n    bounding $\\tau$ requires WMH.\n    Complete barrier diagnosis: all routes reduce to\n    distributional-to-pointwise mixing\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n33 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Adversarial family exact analysis\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:adversarial-affine}):\n    closed-form $\\Lambda_{a,t_{\\min}}=(3/8)^{1-\\{a\\rho\\}}$,\n    $\\theta_{\\mathrm{crit}}=0.01291$;\n    uniform one-step fragility\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:adversarial-fragility})\n  & GPT (theorems) + Claude (verification) \\\\[3pt]\n34 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & General pair-level fragility criterion\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:general-fragility}):\n    $\\beta_B^\\infty + \\lambda_B(1+\\gamma_A)<1$;\n    $75.7\\%$ of $(A,B)$ pairs pass.\n    Exact strong/weak contractor mass split\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:mass-split}):\n    $p_{\\mathrm{weak}} = 0.29436$\n  & GPT (generalization) + Claude (verification) \\\\[3pt]\n35 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Post-Mersenne forced valuation\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:post-mersenne}):\n    after $k$ non-crossing steps from $2^{k+1}{-}1$,\n    $v_{k+1} = 2$ ($k$ even) or $3{+}v_2(k{+}1)$ ($k$ odd);\n    via lifting-the-exponent lemma\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n36 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Burst non-continuation theorem\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:burst-noncontinuation}):\n    after any $k$-step non-crossing burst,\n    $n_k \\equiv 1\\pmod{4}$, forcing $v_{k+1} \\ge 2$;\n    recovery window analysis\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:recovery-window}):\n    adversary can sustain $S/K \\approx 1.0$ over $30{+}$ steps,\n    gap remains open\n  & GPT (conjecture) + Claude (proof \\& refutation) \\\\[3pt]\n37 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Post-burst valuation distribution\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:post-burst-distribution}):\n    $\\Pr(v_{k+1}{=}j) = 2^{1-j}$ for $j \\ge 2$,\n    $\\mathbb{E}[v_{k+1}]{=}3$, independent of $k$\n    and valid for \\emph{all} odd~$m$;\n    non-crossing density threshold\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:v1-density-threshold}):\n    $d^* = 0.708$, orbits safe at $d \\approx 0.58$\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n38 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Weak-recovery cylinder classification\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:weak-recovery-cylinder}):\n    $j$ consecutive $v{=}2$ cycles iff\n    $3^k m \\equiv 1\\pmod{2^{2j}}$;\n    density $2^{-(2j-1)}$, independent of~$k$.\n    Compound pattern bit-counting\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:information-budget}):\n    density $= 2^{-B}$ exact, $B = \\sum\\text{bits}$;\n    information budget flawed due to carry generation\n  & GPT (theorem) + Claude (verification + compound extension) \\\\[3pt]\n39 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Full-cycle uniform-fiber map\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:full-cycle-fiber}):\n    $n_{\\mathrm{exit}}(u) = c_\\tau + 2\\cdot 3^K u$;\n    TV reduction lemma\n    (Lem.~\\ref{lem:tv-reduction}):\n    $\\|\\mu_X - \\nu_X\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}} \\le \\Pr(E_R)$;\n    orbit-level TV summability\n    (Cor.~\\ref{cor:tv-summability}): total TV $\\le 0.028$\n  & GPT (fiber theorem) + Claude (TV reduction, summability) \\\\[3pt]\n40 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Cascade Markov chain on mod~$8$\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:cascade-markov}):\n    deterministic transition table, state~$7$ never exits;\n    $R{=}0$ terminal mechanism\n    (Cor.~\\ref{cor:r0-terminal}): $1/3$ of burst exits\n    end cascade deterministically;\n    episode continuation $q=2/3$, $\\mathbb{E}[L]=3$\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:episode-continuation})\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n41 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Exact cascade PGF\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:cascade-pgf}):\n    $G_{\\mathrm{cas}}(z) = z/(4{-}2z{-}z^2)$,\n    $\\rho = \\sqrt{5}{-}1$,\n    $\\alpha = \\log_2(\\sqrt{5}{-}1) = 0.3058$;\n    spectator-bit propagation\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:spectator-bits}):\n    $\\lfloor (B{-}3)/11.8 \\rfloor$ cycles of IID behavior\n  & Claude (Markov chain PGF) + GPT (compound geometric attempt) \\\\[3pt]\n42 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Exponential tail of $S_{\\mathrm{cycle}}$\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:exponential-tail}):\n    $\\Pr(S>s) \\le C \\cdot 2^{-\\alpha s}$\n    via Cram\\'er--Lundberg;\n    recovery-exit mechanism\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:recovery-exit}):\n    orbit $q \\approx 0.35$, four times stronger than IID\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n43 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Spectator-bit convergence\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:spectator-convergence}):\n    trajectory determined by bottom $\\sim 5$ bits;\n    mod-$32$ uniformity TV $\\le 0.009$ for $B \\ge 16$;\n    orbit $q \\approx 0.33$ uniformly below $2/3$.\n    Gap exit rate correction\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:gap-exit-rates}):\n    IID model pessimistic for gap\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\\begin{table}[!ht]\n\\centering\n\\scriptsize\n\\caption{Contribution attribution (Part 3 of 40).}\n\\label{tab:contributions-3}\n\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.0}\n\\begin{tabular}{@{}clp{8.8cm}p{4.0cm}@{}}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{\\#} & \\textbf{Level} & \\textbf{Contribution} & \\textbf{Primary source} \\\\\n\\midrule\n44 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Self-reinforcing mixing loop\n    (Thm.~\\ref{thm:mixing-loop}):\n    five-step loop closing scrambling $\\to$ uniformity\n    $\\to$ episode bound $\\to$ tail $\\to$ TV $\\to$ refresh;\n    single remaining open step identified\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n45 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Fiber-averaged transition matrix\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:fiber-mixing}):\n    exact $8 \\times 8$ stochastic matrix at resolution~$R$,\n    spectral gap $\\gamma \\ge 0.85$ for $R \\ge 10$,\n    conditional orbit mixing (geometric TV contraction);\n    remaining gap identified as non-divergence\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:residual-conditionality})\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n46 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Corrected cascade PGF verification:\n    independent derivation confirming\n    $G_{\\mathrm{cas}}(z) = z/(4{-}2z{-}z^2)$,\n    $\\mathbb{E}[S] = 5$, $\\rho = \\sqrt{5}{-}1$;\n    coefficient recurrence check through $s = 25$\n  & GPT (independent verification) \\\\[3pt]\n47 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Post-burst continuation bridge\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:post-burst-bridge}):\n    exact geometric law $\\Pr(a_k{=}r) = 2^{-(r-1)}$\n    on burst-exit fibers;\n    $q_{\\mathrm{ep}} = 1/3$ exactly;\n    TV transfer bound\n    $|q_{\\mathrm{ep}}^{\\mathrm{orbit}} - 1/3| \\le \\Pr(\\mathcal{E}_R)$\n  & GPT (theorem + verification) \\\\[3pt]\n48 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Exact rational spectral gap\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:exact-spectral-gap}):\n    explicit $T_{10}$ with entries in $\\mathbb{Q}$,\n    $|\\lambda_2| < 0.146$, $\\gamma > 0.854$;\n    verified by exact characteristic polynomial\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n49 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Non-divergence threshold quantification\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:nondivergence-threshold}):\n    max single-cycle growth $\\approx 8.5$ bits,\n    $43$-bit safety margin for $n_0 \\ge 2^{68}$,\n    Cram\\'er bound $\\Pr(\\text{gain} > 43) \\le 10^{-12}$\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n50 & \\colorbox{red!25}{Critical}\n  & Unconditional mixing structure theorem\n    (Thm.~\\ref{thm:unconditional-mixing}):\n    Collatz conjecture equivalent to\n    ``no orbit gains $43$ bits before spectral\n    contraction engages'';\n    combines Barina verification + exact spectral gap\n    + conditional contraction\n  & Claude \\\\[3pt]\n51 & \\colorbox{red!25}{Critical}\n  & Circularity analysis and true barrier identification\n    (Rem.~\\ref{rem:circularity}):\n    proof chain has one genuine loop\n    (spectator bits $\\leftrightarrow$ exponential tail);\n    single-cycle growth unbounded;\n    Finite Mixing Entry Theorem cannot be proved\n    in current framework;\n    irreducible barrier is carry structure of $3^k n$\n  & Claude (analysis) + GPT (Finite Mixing Entry target) \\\\[3pt]\n52 & \\colorbox{orange!30}{High}\n  & Carry decorrelation\n    (Prop.~\\ref{prop:carry-decorrelation}):\n    burst-length correlation $\\rho